372		 * un-settling promise would keep the epoch marked synced and disarm the
373		 * retry, leaving the dots unreconciled for the life of the connection.
374		 */
375		agentStatusSnapshot: queryProcedure
376			.input(
377				z
378					.object({
379						/**
380						 * (GHOST-TERMINAL) Terminal ids the caller holds dot state for.
381						 * When present, `knownTerminalIds` comes back intersected with
382						 * these instead of listing every row the host has ever minted.
383						 *
384						 * Bounded at the boundary because it feeds `inArray`, which
385						 * expands to one bound parameter per element: past SQLite's
386						 * variable limit the query THROWS, the resync fails, and the
387						 * renderer retries the same oversized input on every reconnect —
388						 * dots frozen for the life of the connection. Rejected rather
389						 * than truncated: a silently shortened candidate list makes the
390						 * sweep treat present terminals as unknown, which is a wrong
391						 * answer dressed as a right one. The renderer sends one id per
392						 * terminal it holds dot state for (tens in practice, one per open
393						 * pane), so 500 is far above anything legitimate and no host-side
394						 * chunking is warranted.
395						 *
396						 * Element LENGTH is deliberately unbounded (min 1 only): the
397						 * creation boundaries accept caller-supplied ids of any length
398						 * (`terminal.createSession` takes a plain string, REST likewise),
399						 * and a length cap here meant one long id with dot state poisoned
400						 * every snapshot query for the host — reconciliation dead on a
401						 * retry loop. SQLite is protected by the ARRAY cap, not element
402						 * size.
403						 */
404						candidateTerminalIds: z.array(z.string().min(1)).max(500).optional(),
405					})
406					.optional(),
407			)
408			.query(async ({ ctx, input }): Promise<AgentStatusSnapshot> => {
409				return buildAgentStatusSnapshot(
410					ctx.terminalAgentStore,
411					ctx.db,
412					input?.candidateTerminalIds,
413				);
414			}),
